    "description": "Daniel in the Lions' Den was painted by the British artist Briton Rivière in 1872 and hangs in the Walker Art Gallery, Liverpool. It shows the prophet Daniel, hands bound, facing the lions after being thrown into their den for continuing to pray (Book of Daniel, chapter 6).",
